 "preferred_name": "Circular economy",
 "kind": "knowledge",
 "definition": "An economic approach that keeps products and materials in use as long as possible through reuse, repair, remanufacturing and recycling, so that waste is designed out.",
 "description": {
  "text": "A model of resource production and consumption based on sharing, leasing, reusing, repairing, refurbishing and recycling to extend product life as long as possible. It aims to tackle climate change, biodiversity loss, waste and pollution.",
